# Triggers on system-owned properties (init.svc.*, sys.*). Under enforcing SELinux init rejects such triggers in
# vendor rc files ("unexported property trigger": vendor_init may not read these properties), so they live here,
# on the system_ext partition, where init may use them without any extra SELinux permission.

# No mpdecision, all CPUs online. Bringing a CPU online while its cpufreq policy is being changed resets this
# SoC (PS_HOLD drop): mpdecision hotplugs 40-60 times a minute under load and its perf locks raise the min
# frequency on every launch and touch. The power HAL applies the boosts itself through sysfs instead.
# Triggered by mpdecision's own service state, so it works however and whenever init.qcom.power.rc starts it.
# msm_thermal core control stays on (offlines cpu1-3 only at 80 C as a last resort).
# init (system) may not write these sysfs files; vendor_init may, so the vendor init.z3tc.rc brings the CPUs
# online on vendor.z3tc.mpdecision_stopped (a trigger fires on every set, also with the same value).
on property:init.svc.mpdecision=running
    stop mpdecision
    setprop vendor.z3tc.mpdecision_stopped 1

# The other system-property triggers of this board (credmgrd, qcamerasvr, swcodec ld.config) are in
# shinano-common init.shinano.system.rc.
